<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brasília Presidential Act</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1998</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brasilia">Brasília</a> Presidential Act was signed on 26 October 1998 by Presidents <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamil-mahuad">Jamil Mahuad</a> of Ecuador and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberto-fujimori">Alberto Fujimori</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, with the guarantor states of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-protocol">Rio de Janeiro Protocol</a>. It fixed the last undemarcated section of their border in the Cordillera del Cóndor, ending a dispute that had caused wars in 1941, 1981 and 1995. Ecuador received a small private property at Tiwinza.</p></div>
